**GROUP FOUR - TASK III (10 marks)**

The C and Pascal programs below are implementations of an algorithm that puts in place a validation rule to ensure that a valid score between 0 and 20 inclusive is input by the user.

**C code**

```c
 1  #include <stdio.h>
 2  int main(void) {
 3    float score;
 4    printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20) ");
 5    scanf("%f", &score);
 6    if ((score < 0) || (score > 20)) {
 7      do {
 8        printf("Enter a valid score please\n");
 9        printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20) ");
10        scanf("%f", &score);
11      } while ((score < 0) || (score > 20));
12    }
13    printf("Valid score entered\n");
14    getchar();
15  }
```

**Pascal code**

```pascal
 1  Program ValidScore;
 2  Var
 3    score: real;
 4  Begin
 5    write('Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20) ');
 6    readln(score);
 7    if ((score < 0) or (score > 20)) then
 8      repeat
 9        writeln('Enter a valid score please');
10        write('Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20) ');
11        readln(score);
12      until ((score < 0) OR (score > 20));
13    writeln('valid score entered');
14    readln;
15  End.
```

(The line numbers are printed in the paper to refer to the lines; they are not part of the programs.)
